diff --git a/docs/operations/vim-nix-local-first.md b/docs/operations/vim-nix-local-first.md
index aaac27e..d51d0bc 100644
--- a/docs/operations/vim-nix-local-first.md
+++ b/docs/operations/vim-nix-local-first.md
@@ -7,11 +7,8 @@ loop.
 ```text
 current source
 → static checks
-→ unpatched controlling-TTY RED
-→ apply the exact test-only patch to a temporary copy
-→ five Canon TDD boundaries
-→ OCI verifier positive/mutation control
-→ optional Herdr exactly-two-pane/clean-stop proof
+→ five focused Canon TDD boundaries
+→ optional Herdr topology probe
 → local Receipt
 → one canonical head
 ```
@@ -27,9 +24,9 @@ Herdr. Supplying the verified Herdr 0.8.0 binary adds an isolated
 server/workspace proof with exactly two panes, process observation, workspace
 close, and clean server stop.
 
-The local runner never edits the tracked smoke implementation. It copies the
-package to a temporary directory and applies the exact test-only patch there.
-Evidence is written under `.local/vim-nix-proof` and excluded from Git.
+The controlling-TTY hand-off is part of the E2E harness itself. The old fake-Vim
+TTY debug test and test-only source patch are intentionally gone. Evidence is
+written under `.local/vim-nix-proof` and excluded from Git.
 
 ## UX contract
 
@@ -49,6 +46,34 @@ Vim exposes no manual history, matcher, route picker, or provider UI. Durable
 history, repeated-decision detection, `command.promoted`, project/shared
 registry projection, policy, and routing remain outside edits.
 
+
+## Focused E2E ownership
+
+```text
+TestAgentFirstChoiceE2E
+  = pre-effect human choice only
+
+TestAgentDecisionSubmitE2E
+  = agent choice -> one typed accepted instruction only
+
+TestExplicitSubmitE2E
+  = generic submit -> draft consumption/undo only
+
+vim-nix runtime lifecycle
+  = accepted -> provider lifecycle -> typed clean stop only
+```
+
+No E2E invokes another E2E. `capture-pty-e2e.sh` only observes
+`TestAgentFirstChoiceE2E/agent_first` and the independent runtime lifecycle at
+already-asserted points; it adds no product behavior.
+
+The originally agreed sequence is only claimed where implementation exists.
+Current focused E2Es cover default Agent choice, explicit direct fallback,
+no pre-submit durable write, typed Agent submit, result lifecycle, and clean
+stop. Worker policy/recovery remain HQ-owned contracts. Automatic completed-
+result rendering in Vim and `command.promoted` projection are not implemented
+by this adapter and are therefore not falsely marked E2E-green here.
+
 ## Deferred high-cost gates
 
 - exact Nix output-closure materialization;
diff --git a/packages/hq-vim/README.md b/packages/hq-vim/README.md
index 4ec2cc4..7882c03 100644
--- a/packages/hq-vim/README.md
+++ b/packages/hq-vim/README.md
@@ -100,16 +100,27 @@ submits the next explicit draft.
 
 ## Canon TDD surface
 
-Only five behavior boundaries remain in this package:
-
-1. minimal editor commands and fail-closed exact HQ binding;
-2. canonical real Vim -> yegappan/lsp -> HQ completion and explicit submit;
-3. native popup: AI-agent first, explicit direct fallback, documentation,
-   Unicode/CRLF edit, one undo, and zero accepted rows before submit;
-4. stale or invalid consumption never destroys a draft;
-5. child Vim retains a controlling TTY when proof output is redirected.
-
-HQ parser/worker/provider tests are intentionally not duplicated here.
+The package keeps five focused behavior boundaries. None is an umbrella E2E:
+
+1. `TestEditorSurfaceAndBindingFailClosed` — the three-command editor surface
+   and exact absolute HQ binding;
+2. `TestAgentFirstChoiceE2E` — real Vim/yegappan/HQ native completion:
+   `agent.exec` first for an empty query, explicit `direct.open` fallback,
+   documentation/undo, and zero durable writes;
+3. `TestAgentDecisionSubmitE2E` — one explicit `HqSubmit` produces exactly one
+   typed Codex instruction. It does not execute the provider;
+4. `TestExplicitSubmitE2E` — one explicit submit appends one accepted row,
+   consumes only the accepted draft, and one Vim undo restores it;
+5. `TestAcceptedSubmitKeepsDraftOnUnsafeConsumption` — stale or invalid
+   consumption never destroys the newer draft.
+
+The separate `vim-nix runtime lifecycle` E2E owns only process/runtime behavior:
+Herdr topology, managed worker readiness, one deterministic provider run,
+`accepted -> started -> stdout -> completed`, typed stop, and zero residual
+processes. It does not re-run the editor choice or submit E2Es.
+
+HQ parser, policy, provider, retry/replay, and promotion tests remain HQ-owned and
+are intentionally not duplicated here.
 
 Run the low-cost suite:
 
@@ -117,14 +128,27 @@ Run the low-cost suite:
 go test ./...
 ```
 
-Run the real popup proof explicitly:
+Run the real choice E2E explicitly:
 
 ```sh
-HQ_NATIVE_HQ_FUZZY_PROOF=1 \
+HQ_AGENT_FIRST_E2E=1 \
 HQ_BIN=/absolute/path/to/hq \
 VIM_EXE=/absolute/path/to/vim \
 VIM9_LSP_PATH=/absolute/path/to/yegappan-lsp \
-go test -run '^TestNativeHQFuzzyAutomaticPopupDoesNotAccept$' -v
+go test -run '^TestAgentFirstChoiceE2E$' -v
+```
+
+### PTY screenshots
+
+Screenshots are an observation projection of the same E2Es, never another test:
+
+```sh
+PROOF_ROOT=/exact/composed/runtime \
+  proofs/vim-nix/capture-pty-e2e.sh
 ```
 
+The capture hook pauses only after the E2E has reached an asserted observable
+state, takes the image, releases the observer, and lets the original E2E finish.
+The receipt records `captureAddsBehavior:false`.
+
 The exact installed Nix/Windows/WSLC proof remains outside this package.
